---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us"
  description="Mindtivate exists to help women navigate their health, relationships, and everyday life with real, evidence-checked information."
>
  <section class="section container prose-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">About Us</p>
    <h1>Knowledge you can actually use</h1>
    <p>
      Mindtivate exists to help women navigate every part of life — body,
      food, mind, hormones, relationships, beauty, sleep, and the stages in
      between — with information that's actually useful, not just
      well-marketed. We're not here to sell you a transformation. We're
      here to answer the question you actually typed into a search bar or
      asked in a community thread at 11pm.
    </p>

    <h2>Why we exist</h2>
    <p>
      So much health and wellness content online is written to sell
      something first and inform second. It's optimized for clicks, not
      for whether the advice actually holds up. Mindtivate is built the
      other way around: we start with the real questions women are asking
      in communities across the internet, and we do the research before we
      write a word.
    </p>

    <h2>What we cover</h2>
    <p>
      Our content spans eight areas of everyday life — Body, Food, Mind,
      Hormones, Love, Beauty, Sleep, and Life Stages — because health
      doesn't live in one category. A hormone shift affects your sleep. A
      bad night's sleep affects your relationships. We try to write about
      that whole picture, not just the fitness-magazine slice of it.
    </p>

    <h2>What we believe</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Practical, specific advice beats vague inspiration.</li>
      <li>Evidence-checked information beats trends and quick fixes.</li>
      <li>You don't need a total life overhaul — small, sustainable changes compound.</li>
      <li>Nothing here replaces a conversation with a qualified provider about your own body.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      If you want the specifics of how an article actually gets made, see
      our <a href={withBase('/about')}>approach</a>. If you want to reach
      us directly, <a href={withBase('/contact')}>get in touch</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose-page {
    max-width: 720px;
  }
</style>
